  {"serve", "start web server using given routes", "Net", "function", 368, "https://github.com/arturo-lang/arturo/blob/v0.9.83/src/library/Net.nim#L368", "routes=function,block", "port=integer:use given port. Default: 18966;silent=logical:don't print info log;chrome=logical:open in Chrome windows as an app", "nothing", "serve .port:18966 [\n    \n    GET \"/\"                     [ \"This is the homepage\" ]\n    GET \"/post\"                 $[id][ \n                                    send.html ~\"This is the post with id: |id|\" \n                                ]                \n    POST \"/getinfo\"             $[id][ \n                                    send.json write.json ø #[\n                                        i: id\n                                        msg: \"This is some info\"\n                                    ] \n                                ]\n]\n\n; run the app and go to localhost:18966 - that was it!\n; the app will respond to GET requests to \"/\" or \"/post?id=...\"\n; and also POST requests to \"/getinfo\" with an 'id' parameterserve $[req][\n    inspect req\n    ;[ :dictionary\n    ;    method   :        GET :string\n    ;    path     :        / :string\n    ;    uri      :        / :string\n    ;    body     :         :string\n    ;    query    :        [ :dictionary\n    ;    ]\n    ;    headers  :        [ :dictionary\n    ;        ...\n    ;    ]\n\n    ; we have to return either a string\n    ; or a dictionary like:\n    #[\n        body: \"...\"\n        status: 200\n        headers: #[\n            ;...\n        ]\n    ]\n]", "name address type description module args attrs returns example line source ", "start web server using given routes", "", "portuse given port. Default: 18966silentdon't print info logchromeopen in Chrome windows as an app", "          usage  serve routes :function :block", "        returns  :nothing", ""},
